A||||14||Songman||My 88 T-top Fiero with only 141 miles.||||12||
Z||000000||Songman||08-20-2001||11:17 PM||||Okay, so it's not really...<P>So, I got these white gauges from BAM-BAM and was going to put them in my car this weekend. As I was cleaning everything up I decided to play with them and popped the odometer out. It took me about 10 minutes of playing with them but I figured out how to set them to 0... Of course, this would be frowned on if I were trying to sell my car as a low mile car or something but I'm not selling it for one, and two, it didn't have the right gauges in it in the first place... plus, my title already says mileage exempt.<P>So today I rode around watching my odometer travel up to 141 miles by the time I got home this evening. When this will really become important is when I redo the car and have the new engine and tranny, paint and interior. Then I'll set it to 0 again.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||12
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||08-20-2001||11:20 PM||||heh, so this is easy to do? I got a spair dash somewhere and I would like to try it.. is it easy to break the damn thing?<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>-Alex<BR>President of Fiero Montreal<BR>86 GT **Silver Stallion**||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||08-20-2001||11:22 PM||||Songman, I hate to tell you this, but it is still a federal offense to tamper with an odometer. I know, it is stupid for old cars.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||08-20-2001||11:27 PM||||  Glad to hear that they worked for ya. Yeah, I have tried the Odometer thing also, just have to be careful not to tear that little pare or plastic strip that holds the counter tabs. Works well though. It is good to know how to do this if you buy a used panel and want to keep your original mileage. Take care Songman   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>PS- Did you get the third brake light yet???<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||08-20-2001||11:27 PM||||Everytime i try to change it the damn thing freaks out when i put it back together and skips numbers up to like 200,000 and all numbers have a chrome space tween them rather than a black one!! How did you avoid that?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroMontreal||08-20-2001||11:27 PM||||heh, yeah but whos gonna go tell the cops..?<P>[picks up phone]Hello 911?...[/picksupphone]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||08-20-2001||11:35 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>Songman, I hate to tell you this, but it is still a federal offense to tamper with an odometer. I know, it is stupid for old cars.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I surely hope they have better things to do that worry about me doing this. It was an experiment for what will basically a new car when it is actually used. And yes, I knew someone would say it is illegal.. hehe... so is driving without a seat belt but I do it...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif">  <P>And yes, it is that easy. Like BAM-BAM said, you just gotta be careful not to break the little green plastic tab that keeps all the notches lined up.. I broke the first one and had to go take one off of another gauge set. I used a jewelers screwdriver and moved it very slightly on each tab till it came off.<P>My odometer was on 145k and change. It was not the original gauges so the Feds can prove to me how many miles are on the car if they want to. Basically you gotta start at the left and just play with it. It will turn through each number to get to 0. Then hold that number and do the next. The trick is to just turn the gear and turn it till it catches. They get the tabs all lined up on the bottom again. Then move to the next one.<P>Fieromaster.. sounds like your tabs aren't all held in place. Mine works perfectly. Actually, I ended up setting mine to 999999.9 and it clicked over when I started driving it. Wonder if the Feds would get upset that I put MORE miles on my car!?<P>Anyway.. as was pointed out this is illegal so DON'T DO IT!<P>And Don, I did get the 3rd brake light. Tim was thrilled! He has just had a wire hanging ever since he got his car. I looked in the box for a tape but didn't find anything... I'm looking forward to hearing some tunes.. I'm sending out the postage I owe you. Hopefully tomorrow if I can keep my cars from breaking down on me!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000007||pontiacs4me||08-20-2001||11:41 PM||||Thats pretty stupid, them getting upset about changing the mileage on the original odometer, on a car that old, I put autometers in my firebird and they come at 00000.0 of course.  I took it to get it inspected (on a trailer) with .2 miles on it and they didnt even question it.  They even put it on the registration that way. But when my title came back it said exempt.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||08-21-2001||12:59 AM||||I've heard that if you write the mileage down, before the rollback, and stick it on the door(like next to the other stickers) it is considered legal.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||08-21-2001||04:15 AM||||One of those things that's blanketly 'illegal' but is only enforced if you attempt to actually defraud someone. (fraud and defruad mean the same thing, I love it! Anyone wanna buy some imflamable refrigerant? ;&gt;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||Phil||08-21-2001||06:49 AM||||Mine was reset to 0 with the engine change 2 years ago(from about 160K) now it only reads 56K. Soon that may change also as I might be installing a set of VDO's that I have||||reg||1
Z||000011||MooCow||08-21-2001||12:17 PM||||I did the same thing to mine songman when I got my 3.4.  The car showed 129,000 and my engine only had 53,000 so I tried to change it busted it cause now it reads 145,000.  So I got a new one and this one I hooked up to a drill set it down and let go threw all the numbers.  It took a while but it worked for me.  wish I would have known the easier way, but o well.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000012||Songman||08-21-2001||12:58 PM||||At least I'll have company in my cell!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroLisa||08-21-2001||01:39 PM||||I changed  the odometer on my coupe- but yah my numbers got all whacked out...It would just jump up a hundred or a thousand randomly. I did sell the car, but the way I did it was just put "Actual Mileage Unknown" on the title, and got in no trouble whatsoever. I told the guy that bought it what the actual mileage was. He was kinda dumb anyway tho.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Butter||08-21-2001||02:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>Songman, I hate to tell you this, but it is still a federal offense to tamper with an odometer. I know, it is stupid for old cars.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well hey Cooter,<BR>Now just what would the government think of this.  While driving my 1967 Ford Fairlane to work one day it clicked over 100000 miles and on those vehicles that meant it went back to 0 miles.  The transmission went out that day and all I had was reverse.  So, instead of a tow bill and more money spent out that was needed to purchase another transmission I backed the car approximately 10 miles back home.  On this model the odometer runs backwards in reverse this put it just back under the 100000 mark for the second time in one day.  In about a week I replaced the transmision and that put it back to 0 miles showing on the odometer in less than one week.  Now was that odometer tampering or just plain hard driving?  After all I did click over the 100000 mark twice on the same car in less than a week.  I come by that situation honestly and just figured the car wanted to be like most folks I know, that is 29 and holding!<P><BR>||||reg||12
